  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ParseOldAtomList",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/FileParsers/MolFileParser.cpp",
    "description": "ParseOldAtomList assumes an old-style atom-list property line has fixed-width fields but performs no minimum-length validation before indexing it. In this PoV, text[4] yields the string terminator for a 4-byte line and selects the invalid-modifier branch; that branch then reads text[14] while constructing the FileParseException message, causing the stack-buffer-overflow. The parser should reject undersized old atom-list lines before any fixed-position access (and the diagnostic should report the actually tested field, text[4], rather than text[14]).",
    "conditions": "The fuzzed bytes are consumed as MolDataStreamToMol options plus the remaining mol stream. A malformed V2000 CTAB is parsed far enough to create at least two atoms, after which ParseMolBlockProperties reads the short line \"  2 \" (4 bytes). Because its first character is not M/A/V/G/S, it is dispatched to ParseOldAtomList. The first three bytes parse as atom index 2 and pass the molecule atom-range check; the missing modifier at offset 4 is interpreted as NUL/default, and error formatting accesses nonexistent offset 14, triggering the out-of-bounds read."
  },
